==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
As there is a Metal Hippoe, it is recommended to bring a fast attacker or a [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]]. [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] does very well on this stage as it can hit the Alien foes (all but the Metal Hippoe) for high damage. It is also possible to cheese this stage by spamming [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cats]].

If you have arrived at this point after collecting all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] don't worry about Elizabeth. Her damage output will be lackluster at 100% strength magnification, to the point at which she can easily be overrun by spammable attackers such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]].

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Don't spawn anything except meatshields until Elizabeth comes out. Wait until all the enemies are at the [[Cat Base]], then send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and continue to spam meatshields. Because the Metal Hippoe is absent from this version of Triton, Bahamut will be able to kill all the enemies without any help.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Since this stage has no restrictions, every unit is fair game. Wait until Kid Tappa gets close to the base and stall him with meatshields, you can use Kid Tappa to stack a few [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cats]] which can Freeze the upcomming threats fairly reliably (don't forget to break his Barrier before they arrive to the front lines. Once stunlocked, send out attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to siphon huge chunks of their HP, and promptly finish them off. If you're struggling with Elizabeth the LVIth's Wave Attacks, Cats with [[Wave Shield]]s, such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], are highly recommended.

